# Ship staging → main

When the user asks to **ship**, **release staging**, **merge staging to main**, or run the full push/PR/merge/sync workflow, use:

```bash
pnpm ship:staging "Commit message here"
```

If changes are already committed:

```bash
pnpm ship:staging --skip-commit
```

Script: `scripts/ship-staging.sh` — commits (optional), pushes `staging`, opens/reuses PR to `main`, waits for CI, **rebase-merges** into `main`, then **resets `staging` to `main`** (no merge-back — staging already had the commits).

PR titles and bodies must follow `git-commits.mdc` — no Cursor / "Made with Cursor" attribution unless the user explicitly approved that wording.

Requires: `gh` CLI authenticated, on `staging` branch (script switches if needed).

Do **not** run this unless the user explicitly requests ship/release/merge to main.
